## Encoding + skeleton notes (READ before quoting Hebrew or Aramaic)

- The staged MT text is **NFC**. Match on a **consonantal skeleton** when a form differs only in vocalisation;
  matching pointed text silently misses forms. A review script that reads Hebrew imports `dan_lib.skeleton` (E-66).
- **The extract carries no maqaf** (646 maqqef segs in the XML, 0 in `../Dan_oshb.txt`). Its whitespace tokens number 5,919,
  equal to the 5,919 main-text words, so maqaf-joined words stand space-separated here. A pattern written with maqaf matches nothing.
- **`dan_lib.skeleton()` DELETES U+05BE.** Its docstring says "maqaf becomes SPACE", but measured on 2026-09-28,
